I've written two task files and the issue responses for this session. The commit step didn't land because git ignores session_plan/, so the files are on disk but not committed. The plan command ends in || true, so the harness seems to expect this.

Task 1: Fixes #1063 (`/bg` door)
• Bug: /bg run 'sleep 600 & echo hi' stays marked "running" until the backgrounded process dies. src/commands_bg.rs reads output to the end before waiting on the shell.
• Fix: wait on the shell first, then give the readers a bounded grace. If a background process still holds the pipe, add a note to the captured output saying the rest wasn't captured.
• Scope: /bg is the last door on #1063 (/run and /watch are already fixed). This slice is in commands, not format, which had 5 of the last 10 changes.
• Required in the work:
  • a failing test before the fix
  • a list of every difference from watch_wait.rs, each marked copied or deliberately different
  • a deliberate break-and-restore check that the new test catches the bug
  • before the push, a grep for every #1063 reference, since "Fixes" will close the ticket

Task 2: Part of #1016 (backlog drain)
• Why this one: the two older items were skipped. #1012 is more price rows in format/, which got a slice at 01:34Z today. #1014's remaining work is a design question, not a 30-minute slice.
• What it does: probes the one row in #1016's last comment that nobody has run. Can a Ctrl+C or other signal drop text the gate already released but the loop hasn't printed yet?
• If text is lost: flush that queued text at teardown, first and once. The flush depends on what text is left, not on which signal fired.
• If nothing is lost: that's still a result. A test pins it, and the reason goes in the commit and on #1016.
• The exit-code row stays open, and the comment says so in those words.

